{"name":"Stardew","hex":"#a6b2b5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Stardew Valley","blocks":[{"text":"Stardew Valley is a 2016 farm life simulation video game developed by Eric \"ConcernedApe\" Barone. Players take the role of a character who inherits their deceased grandfather's dilapidated farm. The game is open-ended, with players managing the farm by clearing land, growing seasonal crops, and raising animals. Players can acquire skills in farming, foraging, fishing, mining, and combat. Social features include building relationships with townspeople, with the option to marry and have a child. A later update added multiplayer, allowing online play with others."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fd/Logo_of_Stardew_Valley.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stardew_Valley"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/96/Stardew_valley_screenshot.png/330px-Stardew_valley_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/96/Stardew_valley_screenshot.png/330px-Stardew_valley_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stardew Valley puts players in charge of managing a farm, taking on tasks such as  growing crops and raising livestock.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStardew_valley_screenshot.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Hackfort_2019_-_Developing_Stardew_Valley_with_Eric_Barone_03.jpg/500px-Hackfort_2019_-_Developing_Stardew_Valley_with_Eric_Barone_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Hackfort_2019_-_Developing_Stardew_Valley_with_Eric_Barone_03.jpg/1280px-Hackfort_2019_-_Developing_Stardew_Valley_with_E